From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vfs: make renameat2() use its directory fds and reject flags

The renameat2() entry in this tree is a stub that calls
sys_renameat(AT_FDCWD, oldname, AT_FDCWD, newname): it ignores both
directory file descriptors and the flags argument.

- renameat2(dirfd, "a", dirfd, "b", 0) with relative names renames in the
  current working directory instead of in dirfd, so it fails with ENOENT
  or moves an unrelated file. bionic implements rename() and renameat()
  on top of renameat2() these days, which is why the LineageOS port
  carries "Revert "Rewrite renameat()."" in bionic.
- renameat2(..., RENAME_NOREPLACE) silently replaces the target and
  RENAME_EXCHANGE silently does a plain rename, where the caller asked
  for the opposite and gets "success" back.

Pass the directory fds through, and return -EINVAL when any flag is set.
That is what mainline does for a filesystem that has no ->rename2
(vfs_rename() in 3.15: "if (flags && !old_dir->i_op->rename2) return
-EINVAL"), and no filesystem here has one. With flags == 0 the call is
now exactly renameat().

Derived from upstream:
  520c8b16505 "vfs: add renameat2 syscall"   (syscall semantics only;
              the ->rename2 plumbing and the flags themselves are not
              backported)

Not compile-tested.
---
 fs/namei.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/namei.c b/fs/namei.c
index af5bf2a..e392c27 100644
--- a/fs/namei.c
+++ b/fs/namei.c
@@ -4118,7 +4118,16 @@ exit:
 SYSCALL_DEFINE5(renameat2, int, olddfd, const char __user *, oldname,
 		int, newdfd, const char __user *, newname, unsigned int, flags)
 {
-	return sys_renameat(AT_FDCWD, oldname, AT_FDCWD, newname);
+	/*
+	 * No filesystem in this tree implements ->rename2, so none of
+	 * RENAME_NOREPLACE, RENAME_EXCHANGE or RENAME_WHITEOUT can be
+	 * honoured. Mainline returns -EINVAL for a filesystem without
+	 * ->rename2 when flags are given, and callers fall back on that.
+	 */
+	if (flags)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	return sys_renameat(olddfd, oldname, newdfd, newname);
 }
 
 SYSCALL_DEFINE2(rename, const char __user *, oldname, const char __user *, newname)
